{"id": "EUVD-2026-82048", "enisaUuid": "073309aa-15b4-3cbd-bc00-fdb0b097c446", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nswiotlb: Preserve allocation virtual address for dynamic pools\n\nswiotlb_alloc_tlb() can allocate from the DMA atomic pool when a decrypted\npool is needed from atomic context. With CONFIG_DMA_DIRECT_REMAP, the\natomic pool is backed by remapped virtual addresses, which are not the same\nas the direct-map addresses returned by phys_to_virt().\n\nswiotlb_init_io_tlb_pool() currently reconstructs the pool virtual address\nfrom the physical start address. For atomic-pool backed allocations this\nstores the wrong address in pool->vaddr. Later, swiotlb_free_tlb() passes\nthat address to dma_free_from_pool(), which will fail to recognize the\nchunk\n\nPass the virtual address returned by the allocation path into\nswiotlb_init_io_tlb_pool(), and store that address in pool->vaddr. This\nkeeps the pool free path using the same virtual address as the allocator.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:50", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68bf3ebd8e7020dae58e8aa14c7d482738bff9a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45507dcb0847e96add4455274b12df0eca6590b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35e0103177826430b5df888b1506239d41e76ab5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1f4d7763cdf1b9e0d35c14aa6f52d0512a36319", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/57d29044d0f29a76c6ec0c112c8c7371d5608dc7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90387", "GHSA-rw87-3jgx-gg57"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14d6da44-87b6-3230-97f5-51ca6e8b1a1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79636caad3618e2b38457f6e298c9b31ba82b489 <45507dcb0847e96add4455274b12df0eca6590b4"}, {"id": "1bf7bf69-0259-3997-957e-bd33673e1b1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79636caad3618e2b38457f6e298c9b31ba82b489 <57d29044d0f29a76c6ec0c112c8c7371d5608dc7"}, {"id": "1c90c65b-e197-3fb7-ab6a-68c3e466b535", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79636caad3618e2b38457f6e298c9b31ba82b489 <68bf3ebd8e7020dae58e8aa14c7d482738bff9a8"}, {"id": "3872099b-c455-358e-8fcd-7344b50cdb3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79636caad3618e2b38457f6e298c9b31ba82b489 <35e0103177826430b5df888b1506239d41e76ab5"}, {"id": "38de7ec6-c90c-3ee8-878a-d57711821a39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "3e72b74c-44d6-3a20-83d2-020105810586", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "79557b74-cb49-3e81-958b-84e12c168d47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a5565435-55f9-3df6-9c1c-6c6eb053b6ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "a641d0eb-0be4-34d5-b743-ae6f3e30067c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b3601d2f-64bc-3635-aa39-0e87bbd38346", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79636caad3618e2b38457f6e298c9b31ba82b489 <c1f4d7763cdf1b9e0d35c14aa6f52d0512a36319"}, {"id": "dc196330-0b7c-30ad-84dc-1876c78e4050", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "fe137881-418f-3bd6-b719-e6b6dfe84dd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5eff7572-5b3f-3a89-afb8-a25873bd95dd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}